{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The sharp points of potsherds</b> — the meaning is: beneath him are sharp potsherds, and he does not feel them." "<b>He spreads</b> — as in רפידתו זהב, and the sense is: he makes a bed." "<b>Harutz</b> — a thing cut down, as in אם חרוצים ימיו, and the meaning is doubled." "<b>Upon the mire</b> — that which is beneath the deep."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:39.572217935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}